config NOVA_FS
	tristate "NOVA: log-structured file system for non-volatile memories"
	depends on FS_DAX
	depends on LIBNVDIMM
	select CRC32
	select LIBCRC32C
	help
	  If your system has a block of fast (comparable in access speed to
	  system memory) and non-volatile byte-addressable memory and you wish
	  to mount a light-weight filesystem with strong consistency support
	  over it, say Y here.

	  To compile this as a module, choose M here: the module will be
	  called nova.

	  If unsure, say N.

choice
	prompt "DeNOVA dedup fingerprint hash"
	depends on NOVA_FS
	default NOVA_DEDUP_HASH_XXHASH
	help
	  Content-fingerprint algorithm used by the offline deduplication
	  daemon. A fingerprint collision can never corrupt data: FACT_insert
	  byte-compares the two candidate blocks before merging them, so a fast
	  non-cryptographic hash is safe here and much cheaper than SHA-1.

	  Note: the on-disk FACT stores fingerprints in this algorithm. Changing
	  it does not corrupt an existing filesystem (byte-verify still applies),
	  but the daemon will not match blocks fingerprinted by the old algorithm
	  until the table is rebuilt with a fresh "mount -o init".

config NOVA_DEDUP_HASH_XXHASH
	bool "xxhash (fast, whole-block avalanche; recommended)"
	select XXHASH
	help
	  128-bit fingerprint from two xxh64 passes. Whole-block avalanche
	  (any single-byte change scrambles all 128 bits), so no single-region
	  collision weakness and no hash-bucket clustering on shared prefixes.
	  ~10x faster than SHA-1. The recommended default.

config NOVA_DEDUP_HASH_CRC32C
	bool "CRC32C (fastest, hardware-accelerated; weaker distribution)"
	select CRC32
	select LIBCRC32C
	help
	  128-bit fingerprint from four hardware CRC32C words (one per 1KB
	  quarter). Fastest option where the CPU has the CRC32 instruction, but
	  a single-quarter difference collides at only 2^-32 and the hash bucket
	  depends only on the first 1KB (prefix clustering). Correctness is still
	  guaranteed by byte-verify; efficiency may suffer on adversarial data.

config NOVA_DEDUP_HASH_SHA1
	bool "SHA-1 (cryptographic, slowest; original DeNOVA behavior)"
	select CRYPTO
	select CRYPTO_HASH
	select CRYPTO_SHA1
	help
	  160-bit cryptographic fingerprint, as in the original DeNOVA. Kept for
	  comparison and for reproducing legacy behavior; far slower than the
	  non-cryptographic options with no correctness benefit now that
	  FACT_insert byte-verifies before merging.

endchoice
